{"id":"25ddd2b9-1e6f-4b4b-95df-66345750bf33","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"af46c5bc6cf36e09","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/commands/ps/ps.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fe4fe03a7d6512220183f874efc48a80750554a1","start":0,"end":54},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","RunInfo","}","from","\"","../../../../shared/runs","\""]},"context":{"after":"0fe3726b1ac55994"}},"payload":{"text":"The terminal's `ps`: the runs (runs.ts) — what the terminals, Run and the tasks started — as a table: a short id (the\nfirst characters of the run's, which `kill` takes), its state, task or service, its port, where it was started, and\nwhat was run. The running ones by default, as `ps` shows live processes; `-a` adds the ones that ended.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:05.926Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:05.926Z"}
